{"rank":2,"title":"Two starting points compete, and the form's own submit button is styled as the lesser one","target":"one filled primary action per view","fix_direction":"Pick one start, usually the prefilled form with its Search button as the single filled primary. Remove the other button or demote it to a text link.","sel":"a.button"}
{"rank":3,"title":"The headline is weaker than the paragraph under it, and the claim that sets this company apart sits at the end of that paragraph","target":"headline the largest and darkest text on the page, a clear step above the lead, contrast of at least 4.5:1, three or four type sizes with real gaps, and the direct-booking claim in the first read","fix_direction":"Make the headline the largest and darkest text, a clear step above the lead, and drop the sizes to three or four with real gaps. Move the direct-booking claim forward, for example by folding the existing words 'book it here with the boatyard that keeps it, no fee on top' into the headline or a line right under it.","sel":"h1"}
{"rank":4,"title":"There is no picture of a boat or the canal","target":"one real photograph of the company's own boats or canal in the hero beside the form","fix_direction":"Add one real photograph of the company's own boats or canal, set into the hero beside the form. The maker must supply the photograph; a stock shot would not do the same job.","sel":null}
{"rank":null,"title":"The route details are gray at 4.46:1, just under the minimum","target":"contrast of at least 4.5:1","fix_direction":"Darken the route details to clear 4.5:1.","sel":"ul > li:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(2)"}
{"rank":null,"title":"38 locks has no point of reference for a first-time hirer","target":"the lock count says what it means for the hirer","fix_direction":"Tell the hirer what the count means for them. This needs a fact only the company has, such as how hard or gentle the week is; the maker must supply it.","sel":"ul > li:nth-of-type(1) > span:nth-of-type(2)"}
{"rank":null,"title":"Routes from Hartwell Junction depends on the Base field but sits far from it","target":"the routes section is near the Base field or visibly tied to it","fix_direction":"Move it nearer the form, or tie it to the form visibly.","sel":"h2"}
{"rank":null,"title":"On widescreen the content is pinned to the two side edges with about 850 px of empty space between","target":"the two columns sit together","fix_direction":"Cap the content width so the two columns sit together.","sel":null}
{"rank":null,"title":"On the phone, route details split a number from its unit","target":"each number stays on the same line as its unit","fix_direction":"Keep the number and its unit together.","sel":"ul > li:nth-of-type(2) > span:nth-of-type(2)"}
{"rank":null,"title":"Start date looks like a plain text field with no calendar cue","target":"the field shows that it is a date picker","fix_direction":"Show that it is a date picker.","sel":"input"}
{"rank":null,"title":"The borders of the input and select fields look pale against the white card","target":"border contrast of at least 3:1 against the card","fix_direction":"Measure the borders against 3:1, and darken them if they fall short.","sel":"input"}
{"rank":null,"title":"On the tablet the lead paragraph ends with hire. alone on its last line","target":"no one-word last line in the lead paragraph","fix_direction":"Rebalance the lines so the last line holds more than one word.","sel":"p.lead"}

